  "assessment": {
    "rationale": "This parent grid-envelope simulation is mostly about envelope shape, variant inventory, and successor boundaries, not chunk-feed replication or duplicate peer advertisements. It aligns reasonably with PromiseGrid goals through explicit non-central, specimen-first, durable framing, but it gives little direct guidance on whether duplicate offers are harmless or how Bob chooses between Alice and Carol without turning feeds into reputation infrastructure.",
    "strengths": [
      "Explicitly avoids premature central authority and canonicalization.",
      "Good audit trail and lineage across candidate variants and decisions.",
      "Clear boundary between parent inventory and concrete successor specimens."
    ],
    "weaknesses": [
      "Does not model chunk offers, advertisements, or peer-choice logic.",
      "Little direct failure handling for duplicate or conflicting advertisements.",
      "Uses limited promise-first payload vocabulary."
    ],
    "risks": [
      "Envelope work could be over-applied to feed-selection problems it does not solve.",
      "Open signature and identity questions leave duplicate-advertisement accountability underspecified."
    ],
    "open_questions": [
